  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>edoxaban</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>B01AF03</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, oral dosing <small>(PK_2C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Zou P et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>pediatric patients</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>edoxaban</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_edoxaban/Edoxaban_Zou2025_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Apparent clearance, CL/F (L/h) a</td><td>42.87</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>Absorption rate constant, Ka (1/h)</td><td>3.71</td><td>1/h</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr><tr><td>Apparent central compartment volume, Vc/F (L)</td><td>261</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>Apparent inter‐compartmental clearance, Q/F (L/h)</td><td>8.59</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>Apparent peripheral compartment volume, Vp/F (L)</td><td>343.5</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>Transit rate constant, Ktr (1/h)</td><td>47.5</td><td>1/h</td><td><small>ktr</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q22_egfr</td><td>0.268</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr></table><h4>About edoxaban</h4><p>Edoxaban is a direct factor Xa inhibitor used to prevent stroke in atrial fibrillation and to treat venous thromboembolism such as pulmonary embolism. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union, and is widely used as an anticoagulant.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21011234\">Wikidata Q21011234</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Edoxaban\">Edoxaban</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Zou P et al. (2025). Population pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of edoxaban in pediatric patients. <i>CPT: pharmacometrics &amp; systems pharmacology 14(1):118–129</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/psp4.13248\">10.1002/psp4.13248</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39526427\">39526427</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Zou_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
